<%# The Verto's UN SDG tags (surveys.sdgs, derived by SdgClassifier), as small
    neutral chips beside the status badges. Untagged Vertos render nothing —
    "no goal applies" is a quiet verdict, not a state to advertise.

    Capped at three chips plus a "+N" overflow whose tooltip lists the rest, so
    a broadly-tagged Verto can't crowd the badge row off the tile.

    Chip text is "SDG n" — the UN's own locale-independent shorthand — and the
    tooltip carries the official goal title, a proper noun served from UnSdgs.
    Deliberately no locale strings in v1 (vs CLAUDE.md's all-19-files rule):
    nothing here is translatable UI chrome. If that changes, the upgrade path
    is a `sdg.goals.*` namespace mirrored across all 19 files. %>
<% sdgs = survey.sdgs %>
<% if sdgs.any? %>
  <% chip_style = "font-family:'Alata',sans-serif;font-size: var(--text-2xs);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.10);color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75);backdrop-filter:blur(4px);white-space:nowrap;" %>
  <% shown, overflow = sdgs.first(3), sdgs.drop(3) %>
  <% shown.each do |n| %>
    <span title="<%= UnSdgs.title(n) %>" style="<%= chip_style %>"><%= UnSdgs.label(n) %></span>
  <% end %>
  <% if overflow.any? %>
    <span title="<%= overflow.map { |n| UnSdgs.label_with_title(n) }.join(", ") %>" style="<%= chip_style %>">+<%= overflow.size %></span>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
